Relevant columns, their usage & likely conditions  
• “week”: filter rows to the date window ‘2024‑09‑01’ ≤ week ≤ ‘2024‑09‑14’ and to make sure it is a weekday (Mon‑Fri).  
• “rank”: keep only the values 1, 2, 3 (top three).  
• “term”: the actual Google‑search text that we finally want to show.  
• “refresh_date”: the snapshot date we have to group by and show in reverse chronological order.  
• “dma_id / dma_name / score”: not required for the requested result, but useful while exploring and validating.

Typical WHERE clauses that will be re‑used  
WHERE  
    "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'  
    AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)  
    AND TO_CHAR("week",'DY') NOT IN ('SAT','SUN')      -- Monday‑Friday only  

Below are ten progressively richer Snowflake SELECT statements (LIMIT 20 each) to inspect the data and build toward the final answer.  Adjust or remove LIMIT when you are ready for the full result set.

```sql
-- 1) Description: quick look at the date window to be sure data exists.
