Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, their usage & likely conditions  
• “week”: filter rows to the date window ‘2024‑09‑01’ ≤ week ≤ ‘2024‑09‑14’ and to make sure it is a weekday (Mon‑Fri).  
• “rank”: keep only the values 1, 2, 3 (top three).  
• “term”: the actual Google‑search text that we finally want to show.  
• “refresh_date”: the snapshot date we have to group by and show in reverse chronological order.  
• “dma_id / dma_name / score”: not required for the requested result, but useful while exploring and validating.

Typical WHERE clauses that will be re‑used  
WHERE  
    "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'  
    AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)  
    AND TO_CHAR("week",'DY') NOT IN ('SAT','SUN')      -- Monday‑Friday only  

Below are ten progressively richer Snowflake SELECT statements (LIMIT 20 each) to inspect the data and build toward the final answer.  Adjust or remove LIMIT when you are ready for the full result set.

```sql
-- 1) Description: quick look at the date window to be sure data exists.
SELECT *
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: distinct weeks inside the window to verify weekday coverage.
SELECT DISTINCT "week"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
ORDER BY "week"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: look only at Monday–Friday records by checking day name.
SELECT "week",
       TO_CHAR("week",'DY') AS "day_of_week",
       "term",
       "rank"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND TO_CHAR("week",'DY') NOT IN ('SAT','SUN')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: verify that rank holds small integers & confirm the top 3.
SELECT DISTINCT "rank"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
ORDER BY "rank"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: show the terms that have rank 1, 2, or 3 on weekdays.
SELECT "week",
       "term",
       "rank"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND TO_CHAR("week",'DY') NOT IN ('SAT','SUN')
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
ORDER BY "week","rank"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: check whether multiple refresh_date snapshots exist for the same week.
SELECT DISTINCT "week", "refresh_date"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
ORDER BY "week" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: list rank 1–3 terms with their refresh_date, still limited for inspection.
SELECT "refresh_date",
       "week",
       "rank",
       "term"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND TO_CHAR("week",'DY') NOT IN ('SAT','SUN')
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC, "week", "rank"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: use DISTINCT to avoid duplicates if the same term repeats for a rank / refresh_date.
SELECT DISTINCT "refresh_date",
       "week",
       "rank",
       "term"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND TO_CHAR("week",'DY') NOT IN ('SAT','SUN')
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC, "rank"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: group by refresh_date and week, collect the three terms into a list (array) for each day.
SELECT "refresh_date",
       "week",
       ARRAY_AGG("term" ORDER BY "rank") AS "top_three_terms"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND TO_CHAR("week",'DY') NOT IN ('SAT','SUN')
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
GROUP BY "refresh_date", "week"
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10) Description: FINAL retrieval – top three terms for each weekday, grouped by refresh_date and ordered newest‑first.
SELECT "refresh_date",
       "week",
       "rank",
       "term"
FROM "GOOGLE_TRENDS"."GOOGLE_TRENDS"."TOP_TERMS"
WHERE "week" BETWEEN '2024-09-01' AND '2024-09-14'
  AND TO_CHAR("week",'DY') NOT IN ('SAT','SUN')
  AND "rank" IN (1,2,3)
ORDER BY "refresh_date" DESC, "rank"
LIMIT 20;
```
